From 6e2d5928a6315a9445fd615ae8a44e45addec557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:56:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild the gallery: album pages, thumbnails, bulk upload

Public pages
- Gallery page now lists albums as cover cards (paginated); each album
  opens on its own page, so only one album's images are ever requested.
- Grid tiles use resized Cloudinary thumbnails (600x450, q_auto, f_auto)
  and the lightbox a 1600px version, instead of the full-size originals.
- Images are lazy-loaded with explicit dimensions; large albums show 24
  tiles at a time with a Load more button.
- Videos get a real poster frame and a play icon.
- Hero image converted from a 1.1 MB PNG to a 186 KB WebP.

Admin
- New "Upload photos and videos" button on an album: many files at once,
  sent straight from the browser to Cloudinary (signed), so large videos
  no longer pass through the web server and hit its request timeout.
- Albums get a cover image and an order field; photos and videos get an
  order field and a thumbnail preview in the admin.

Adds migration 0004, Greek translations for the new strings, and tests.

